tor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The curl version lock was directly exercised against a newer available build and persisted across reboot. RHEL 9.8 and the original kernel were preserved. The mandatory restart protocol is strong: it records healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot scheduling, a changed boot identity, restored curl functionality and lock behavior, and matching lifecycle boot-identity observations.","limitations":["No full system-wide update was executed; update protection was demonstrated with targeted `dnf upgrade curl` attempts against a directly observed newer candidate.","The restart evidence contains no separate application data or cluster-state probe because this is a single-node package-management task with no task-specific application data or cluster service. Package state, executable functionality, platform state, and package-manager health were recovered and observed."]}
